If you mean pushing a boulder towards a pit that has a monster
in it, no, this won't auto-squish the monster.  In fact, weirdly
enough, the monster is injured by the falling boulder, but if
he is not killed by it, he stays in the pit (with the boulder
somehow hanging above him) until he dies. Then the boulder
falls and fills the pit.

With great effort you move the boulder.
The boulder falls into the pit.  The boulder hits it.  The gnome hits!
The gnome hits!
You kill the gnome!  The boulder fills a pit.





